.TH HANOI 1
.SH NAME
hanoi \- Towers of Hanoi animation
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B temple/hanoi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I Hanoi
is a port of the TempleOS
.B Demo/Graphics/Hanoi.HC
Towers of Hanoi animation.
It runs under
.IR wm (1).
.PP
Six disks move automatically among three poles, the animation of each
move sitting inside the classic three-line recursion.  The readout at the
top left \- \fIDisk: n from p to q\fP \- is that recursion talking, so
the disk numbers it names run large-to-small as the stack unwinds.  Two
beeps when it finishes.  Enter restarts it.
.PP
The disks take their colours from
.B gr_rainbow_10
(Adam/Gr/GrPalette.HC), so the smallest disk on top is black.
.PP
The controls are:
.TF space
.TP
.B Enter / r
Restart animation
.TP
.B Esc / q
Quit
.PD
.SH SOURCE
.B /appl/temple/hanoi.b
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR temple (1),
.IR tone (2),
.IR wm (1)
